    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nI can't get `MiniAnimateNormalFloat` hlg to be respected\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. `:vsp`\r\n\r\n`minimal.lua`:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal root = vim.fn.fnamemodify(\"./.repro\", \":p\")\r\nfor _, name in ipairs({ \"config\", \"data\", \"state\", \"cache\" }) do\r\n    vim.env[(\"XDG_%s_HOME\"):format(name:upper())] = root .. \"/\" .. name\r\nend\r\nlocal lazypath = root .. \"/plugins/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n    vim.fn.system({ \"git\", \"clone\", \"--filter=blob:none\", \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\", lazypath, })\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.runtimepath:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\nlocal plugins = {\r\n    {\r\n        \"echasnovski/mini.animate\",\r\n        version = \"*\",\r\n        config = function()\r\n            local animate = require(\"mini.animate\")\r\n            animate.setup {\r\n                open = {\r\n                    timing = animate.gen_timing.linear({ duration = 2000, unit = 'total' }),\r\n                    winconfig = animate.gen_winconfig.wipe({ direction = 'from_edge' }),\r\n                    winblend = animate.gen_winblend.linear({ from = 0, to = 100 }),\r\n                },\r\n                close = {\r\n                    timing = animate.gen_timing.linear({ duration = 2000, unit = 'total' }),\r\n                    winconfig = animate.gen_winconfig.wipe({ direction = 'to_edge' }),\r\n                    winblend = animate.gen_winblend.linear({ from = 100, to = 0 }),\r\n                },\r\n            }\r\n        end\r\n    },\r\n}\r\n\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup(plugins, {\r\nroot = root .. \"/plugins\",\r\n})\r\n\r\nvim.o.termguicolors = true\r\n\r\nvim.cmd[[hi MiniAnimateNormalFloat guibg=green]]\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI would expect the highlight group to be respected.\r\n\r\nIt works, when I set `NormalFloat`, but I can't do this because it is used by many other floating windows.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/16707112/624e2a66-b351-49f6-9982-a63cf05ed748\r\n\r\n",
